---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="DeckMirror // Vivaldi Workspace & Tab Synchronizer — PULSAR Suite">
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="relative pt-16 pb-20 px-4 lg:px-8 border-b border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Ambient Glow -->
    <div class="absolute top-1/4 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-[600px] h-[600px] bg-emerald-500/10 rounded-full blur-[120px] pointer-events-none"></div>

    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto text-center relative z-10">
      <!-- Promo Banner -->
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8">
        <div class="border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-950/20 px-4 py-2 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-3 text-xs">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 border border-emerald-400/40 text-emerald-400 font-mono font-semibold text-[10px] uppercase">Pulsar Matrix</span>
            <span class="text-slate-300 text-[11px]">Free & Open-Source Browser Tool</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-slate-400 font-mono text-[10px]">Polar Tip Jar:</span>
            <a href="https://buy.polar.sh/polar_cl_DrOMaecRuEdvn8seYYegzMt0jEDbuY92X4zMd2NkGD8" target="_blank" class="px-2.5 py-0.5 bg-emerald-500 text-black font-mono font-semibold text-[10px] uppercase hover:bg-emerald-400 transition-colors">
              ☕ Buy Coffee
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Spec Pill -->
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-slate-400 text-[11px] font-mono mb-8 tracking-wider">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
        <span>ABTEILUNG83 // SPECIFICATION_DECKMIRROR</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Hero Title -->
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white uppercase mb-6 leading-[1.05]">
        DECKMIRROR
      </h1>
      
      <p class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm sm:text-base tracking-wide uppercase mb-6">
        Cross-Device Vivaldi Workspace & Tab Synchronizer
      </p>

      <p class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Browse and mirror your Vivaldi browser workspaces and open tabs across all your machines via any folder you already sync (Dropbox, iCloud Drive, Syncthing). Zero accounts. Zero servers. 100% privacy.
      </p>

      <!-- Action Buttons -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 mb-16 font-mono text-xs">
        <a href="#install" class="px-6 py-3 bg-emerald-500 hover:bg-emerald-400 text-black font-bold tracking-wider uppercase transition-colors shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20">
          ⚡ Install Extension
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/aeon022/WorkspaceSync" target="_blank" class="px-6 py-3 bg-white/5 hover:bg-white/10 border border-white/20 text-white font-medium tracking-wider uppercase transition-colors">
          View GitHub Repository
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Hero Visual Art Container -->
      <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto monolith-card p-4 sm:p-6 mb-12">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        
        <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-6 text-left">
          <div class="w-48 h-48 shrink-0 rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-emerald-500/30 shadow-2xl relative">
            <img src="./deckmirror-hero.png" alt="DeckMirror App Icon" class="w-full h-full object-cover">
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[10px] text-emerald-400 mb-2">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-ping"></span>
              <span>LIVE PEER-TO-PEER CONVERGENCE</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2 font-mono">Real-time Workspace Bridging</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Vivaldi workspaces stay segregated by design. DeckMirror bridges your active browser sessions across devices without third-party servers by reading and writing atomic snapshots into your private sync folder.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 font-mono text-[10px]">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-slate-300">macOS UI Hook</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-slate-300">File System Access API</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-slate-300">Selective Mirroring</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 4 Structural Metrics -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto text-left">
        <div class="monolith-card p-5">
          <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mb-2 font-mono tracking-wider">METRIC_01</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-1">LOCAL SYNC</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">NO SERVER / NO CLOUD</div>
        </div>
        <div class="monolith-card p-5">
          <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mb-2 font-mono tracking-wider">METRIC_02</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-1">REAL-TIME</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">EVENT-DRIVEN ENGINE</div>
        </div>
        <div class="monolith-card p-5">
          <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mb-2 font-mono tracking-wider">METRIC_03</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-1">LAYER 2</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">VIVALDI WORKSPACE HOOK</div>
        </div>
        <div class="monolith-card p-5">
          <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
          <div class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mb-2 font-mono tracking-wider">METRIC_04</div>
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-300 mb-1">0% TRACKING</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">100% PRIVATE & OFFLINE</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Features Matrix -->
  <section id="features" class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-8 py-20">
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-white/10 pb-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider">01 // CORE ARCHITECTURE</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Three Modes of Synchronicity</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <!-- Feature 1 -->
      <div class="monolith-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div>
          <div class="text-2xl mb-4 text-emerald-400 font-mono">01. BROWSE</div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Explore Remote Tabs</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            See all workspaces and tabs open on your other machines in your Vivaldi sidepanel. Click any tab to launch it locally, or click "Open All" to open an entire workspace instantly.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-white/10 text-[11px] font-mono text-emerald-400">
          Read-only · Zero local impact
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 2 -->
      <div class="monolith-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div>
          <div class="text-2xl mb-4 text-cyan-400 font-mono">02. PUBLISH</div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Selective Sync Control</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Decide exactly which workspaces get shared. Uncheck sensitive workspaces (e.g. "Banking" or "Private") to prevent them from ever leaving your local machine.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-white/10 text-[11px] font-mono text-cyan-400">
          Per-workspace opt-in
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 3 -->
      <div class="monolith-card p-6 flex flex-col justify-between">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div>
          <div class="text-2xl mb-4 text-purple-400 font-mono">03. MIRROR</div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Active Tab Convergence</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Enable Mirror on two machines with matching workspace names. Open and close tabs on one device and watch them automatically reflect on the other within seconds.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-white/10 text-[11px] font-mono text-purple-400">
          Bi-directional live convergence
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Architecture Deep-Dive -->
  <section id="architecture" class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-8 py-16 border-t border-white/10">
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-white/10 pb-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider">02 // TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">How DeckMirror Works</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 font-mono text-xs">
      <div class="monolith-card p-6">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div class="text-emerald-400 font-bold mb-3 text-sm">LAYER 1 — MV3 EXTENSION</div>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Runs inside Vivaldi's extension sandbox with a Manifest V3 Service Worker. Manages the File System Access API handle to read and write peer snapshots into your shared sync folder.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>▸</span> Real-time tab lifecycle event hooks</li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>▸</span> Conflict-free timestamped cursor sync</li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>▸</span> Persistent local handle preservation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="monolith-card p-6">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div class="text-cyan-400 font-bold mb-3 text-sm">LAYER 2 — VIVALDI UI HOOK</div>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Standard extensions cannot read Vivaldi's internal workspace assignments. Layer 2 is a lightweight script injected into Vivaldi's privileged UI frame, writing accurate tab-to-workspace mappings.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>▸</span> Direct access to Vivaldi <code class="text-white">vivExtData</code></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>▸</span> Reads real user workspace labels & IDs</li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span>▸</span> Dynamic lifecycle coupling via Management API</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Installation Section -->
  <section id="install" class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-8 py-16 border-t border-white/10">
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-white/10 pb-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider">03 // GETTING STARTED</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Installation & Setup</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="monolith-card p-6">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-white mb-3">
          <span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-emerald-500 text-black text-xs">STEP 1</span>
          <span>Clone & Load Extension in Vivaldi</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-black/50 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-slate-300 border border-white/10 rounded mb-3">
          git clone https://github.com/aeon022/WorkspaceSync.git DeckMirror
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
          Open <code class="text-emerald-400">vivaldi://extensions</code> → Enable <strong>Developer Mode</strong> → Click <strong>Load unpacked</strong> and select the DeckMirror directory.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="monolith-card p-6">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-white mb-3">
          <span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-emerald-500 text-black text-xs">STEP 2</span>
          <span>Select your Shared Sync Folder</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
          Open the DeckMirror <strong>Options</strong> page and pick a folder inside your cloud sync service (Dropbox, iCloud Drive, or Syncthing). Pick the exact same folder on every device.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="monolith-card p-6">
        <span class="tick-tl">+</span><span class="tick-tr">+</span><span class="tick-bl">+</span><span class="tick-br">+</span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-white mb-3">
          <span class="px-2 py-0.5 bg-emerald-500 text-black text-xs">STEP 3</span>
          <span>Inject Layer 2 UI Hook (macOS)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-black/50 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-slate-300 border border-white/10 rounded mb-3">
          bash scripts/inject-uimod.sh
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
          Fully restart Vivaldi (⌘Q) to activate workspace name recognition and real-time active tab mirroring.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <section id="faq" class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-8 py-16 border-t border-white/10">
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-white/10 pb-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider">04 // FAQ</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 font-mono text-xs">
      <div class="monolith-card p-5">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Does DeckMirror send any data to external servers?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          No. DeckMirror contains zero network calls, zero telemetry, and zero tracking. All synchronization happens via local JSON snapshot files placed in your chosen folder.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="monolith-card p-5">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Does Mirroring close my existing tabs when turned on?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          No. Mirroring never performs retroactive destructive merges. When you first enable Mirror for a workspace, it anchors the current cursor timestamp and only replicates new tab opens and closes from that moment forward.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="monolith-card p-5">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Is DeckMirror compatible with other Chromium browsers?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Layer 1 (Browse and Sync tabs) works across Chromium browsers (Brave, Edge, Chrome, Arc). The deep workspace detection (Layer 2) is purpose-built for Vivaldi's workspace architecture.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
